WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.846 --> 00:00:03.923
In hall B a motor turns the belt of line 3.

2
00:00:04.605 --> 00:00:05.917
A compressor makes air.

3
00:00:06.618 --> 00:00:08.882
Both get their power from the switchboard.

4
00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:12.089
Power is the rate of using energy.

5
00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:14.838
Four topics follow that story.

6
00:00:15.559 --> 00:00:18.067
First the power and the motor that uses it.

7
00:00:19.165 --> 00:00:24.099
Then how you start and control the motor, and the compressed air and the hydraulics.

8
00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:28.802
The first topic is Electricity and energy in the plant.

9
00:00:29.607 --> 00:00:34.135
The energy bill counts kilowatt-hours and the grid connection counts kilowatts.

10
00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:38.553
Efficiency is how much of the power is left as motion.

11
00:00:39.226 --> 00:00:40.619
The rest becomes heat.

12
00:00:41.695 --> 00:00:44.783
On the nameplate of the motor you read the rated power.

13
00:00:46.082 --> 00:00:48.485
The second topic is Electric motors.

14
00:00:49.223 --> 00:00:53.437
The belt of line 3 has an induction motor, like most conveyors.

15
00:00:54.442 --> 00:00:57.112
The stator makes a rotating magnetic field.

16
00:00:57.902 --> 00:01:02.615
That field drags the rotor along, and the rotor always runs a little slower.

17
00:01:03.653 --> 00:01:06.265
Many motors run at half load or less.

18
00:01:06.993 --> 00:01:11.324
With a clamp meter round one cable you see what the motor really draws.

19
00:01:12.618 --> 00:01:15.010
The third topic is Starting and drives.

20
00:01:15.766 --> 00:01:20.329
A motor switched straight on draws 6 to 8 times its rated current.

21
00:01:21.388 --> 00:01:25.115
A soft starter ramps the voltage up over a few seconds.

22
00:01:25.851 --> 00:01:27.732
That cuts the spike and the jolt.

23
00:01:28.827 --> 00:01:32.670
A VFD changes the frequency and so the speed, smoothly.

24
00:01:33.373 --> 00:01:36.647
That lets the belt of line 3 run faster or slower.

25
00:01:37.977 --> 00:01:41.030
The fourth topic is Compressed air and hydraulics.

26
00:01:41.737 --> 00:01:45.870
Compressed air is the most expensive way to deliver energy in a plant.

27
00:01:46.692 --> 00:01:50.802
Around 10 percent does useful work and the rest becomes heat.

28
00:01:51.876 --> 00:01:53.281
Leaks are the big loss.

29
00:01:54.015 --> 00:01:59.158
Without a leak programme often 20 to 30 percent of the compressor output escapes.

30
00:02:00.175 --> 00:02:03.844
With a leak test you measure at the weekend, with production stopped,

31
00:02:04.030 --> 00:02:05.586
how much air leaks away.

32
00:02:06.599 --> 00:02:11.661
Hydraulics uses oil under high pressure to make large forces in a small space.

33
00:02:12.946 --> 00:02:13.793
The whole map.

34
00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:19.683
Motors, drives and fluid power is the fourth station of Energy and the grid.

35
00:02:20.734 --> 00:02:22.464
Every topic has four levels.

36
00:02:23.483 --> 00:02:27.187
Start with Power, energy and three-phase at Basics level.

37
00:02:27.886 --> 00:02:31.148
That lesson explains kilowatts and kilowatt-hours.

38
00:02:32.206 --> 00:02:35.503
At Working knowledge level it is about energy per product,

39
00:02:35.642 --> 00:02:38.545
motor load, speed control and hydraulics.

40
00:02:39.538 --> 00:02:42.162
At Advanced level it is about power factor,

41
00:02:42.324 --> 00:02:45.099
motor protection, harmonics and air quality.

42
00:02:46.104 --> 00:02:50.480
At Expert level it is about energy baselines, repair or replace,

43
00:02:50.713 --> 00:02:52.733
drive systems and safe design.

44
00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:57.940
Every lesson and every film in this module has a place on this map.
